        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIAs">VI As</ref> Inscr.</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="VI As. Inscr." corresp="#wit-q">Decretum episcoporum et aliorum sapientum London'.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="VI As. Inscr." corresp="#wit-h">Iudicia ciuitatis Lundonię.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h">Iudicia Civitatis Lundoniæ</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h">[Decrees of the city of London]</ab>
        <note type="editorial">The Latin is the Quadripartitus; Liebermann's Old English is from H (Textus Roffensis f. 88, after ‘Exceptiones ex decretis pontificum’). H's Latin heading is in red and not Æthelstanian. Liebermann prints no German for the heading.</note>
      </div>
